Z||000000||Eric_PA||07-25-2000||12:07 PM||||Hi, I was wondering if anybody out there knew what the Special Touring Edition represented on the 86 1/2 Fastback? Thanks in advance. <P>Eric<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||07-25-2000||02:42 PM||||I'm guessing it's a dealer-installed option package, because I have never before heard of a Fiero STE.  Where did you see one?||||reg||5
Z||000002||fiero56||07-25-2000||06:07 PM||||I just read this again, and it reminded me of my Fiero MotorWeek video. In the video, they are talking about the v-6 engine in the Fiero being similar to the engine in the Pontiac 6000 STE. For those with the video, this is mentioned while the '85GT is being track tested(I think). Might just mean v-6? I don't know. Just a thought.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||07-25-2000||08:26 PM||||Sounds like it may be a "decal" Special Editon, special cuz the decal says so. What kind of options does it have? Could be an option package specially desigated for a particular region or dealership group.<P>Mrs. stimpy thinks it's "Stick-it To Everyone"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ezsurf||07-25-2000||10:01 PM||||Ed Parks told me that was about the only thing different on the special edition.  If there is anything else different, he didn't mention it.  I didn't know there was an official special edition until I went to the Fiero Factory, and there was one in the shop.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||07-25-2000||10:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ezsurf:<BR>Ed Parks told me <B>that</B> was about the only thing different on the special edition.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What is "that"? I'm dyin of suspense here!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric_PA||07-25-2000||11:03 PM||||I own this Fiero Gt with the STE emblems. They are located on the door panels in the car above the arm rests. The options with the car are as follows. 86 1/2 Fastback, black with grey rocker panels, automatic, power windows/mirrors, spoiler, sunroof. Nothing seems different from any other Fiero. Would really like to know what it means though. Thanks so far guys.<P><BR>I can take a digital picture of it, but how do you post pics on here? I guess I could email it if anybody would like to see what it looks like.<P>Thanks,<BR>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gold-86SE||07-26-2000||10:09 AM||||<BR>Since you guys are talking about STE labels, let me throw in another question.<P>Has anyone ever seen a Fiero labeled "Fiero SE/GT 6" on the rear deck lid?<P>My Fiero has this labeling and the SE/GT is red, and is also located on the front and on the door posts.<P>This is my Gold 86 SE V6 4-spd.<P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||07-26-2000||10:12 AM||||Could they (i.e., GM) be referring to the mid year change from the notchback GT to the fast back GT?<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000009||Gold-86SE||07-26-2000||10:16 AM||||<BR>I have consider that, but everyone that I have ever spoken with has told me it is a fluke, an aftermarket change, I wish I knew. Is there any way to find out for sure?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||07-26-2000||10:21 AM||||The STE and the SE/GT emblems may be dealer installed nameplates. I know that some dealers would add stuff onto a car to raise the price of it. I know a dealer by me back in 86 had a black Fiero coupe (4cyl/5spd) with the Kamei aero kit on it. They had painted on the decklid and on the aeroskirts "Fiero SS".<BR>Then they tacked on $3500.00! (kit at the time was $600)<BR>Back then dealers use to add stuff to vehicles to sell them for a higher price. I remember many places adding pinstripes and charging $1500.00 or more!||||reg||1
Z||000011||Gold-86SE||07-26-2000||10:33 AM||||<BR>I believe that my Fiero may have been sold in Florida and during it's life made it to Tejas, because under the window tinting there is a sticker advertising the installer.<P>Is there a way to track down the original dealership?<P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||1
